[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi,<br>\nI want to formalize the apolarity lemma in commutative algebra. This is a stepping stone toward proving the celebrated theorem about the Waring rank of a monomial (<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1110.0745\">https://arxiv.org/pdf/1110.0745</a>).</p>\n<p>I'm fairly new to Lean, so I have a few questions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Is the level of abstraction in the paper acceptable in Mathlib4? This is the proof that I know, but I imagine it could be stated in a more abstract way.</li>\n<li>How can I check whether this lemma isn't a consequence of some other, more abstract already-formalized theorem?</li>\n<li>Is there anything else I should consider while working on this?</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Also, if anyone is interested in collaborating to write the proof together, that would be very cool :)</p>",
        "id": 611466229,
        "sender_full_name": "Aviv Bar-Natan",
        "timestamp": 1784408180
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"971443\">Aviv Bar-Natan</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Formalizing.20the.20apolarity.20lemma/near/611466229\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<ol>\n<li>Is the level of abstraction in the paper acceptable in Mathlib4? This is the proof that I know, but I imagine it could be stated in a more abstract way.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can you state the lemma using Mathlib? If not, what definitions are missing?</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"971443\">Aviv Bar-Natan</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Formalizing.20the.20apolarity.20lemma/near/611466229\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li>Is there anything else I should consider while working on this?</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n<p>PRs should be small, and the sooner you can PR something the sooner you can get feedback to align your style with Mathlib</p>",
        "id": 611466763,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1784408713
    },
