    {
        "content": "<ul>\n<li><code>pderiv_comm</code> looks useful and missing</li>\n<li>Could the ideal be defined on a set of polynomials, similar to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MvPolynomial.vanishingIdeal#doc\">docs#MvPolynomial.vanishingIdeal</a> ?</li>\n<li>The definition of <code>apolarHom</code> seems awkward; could using <code>Derivation</code> or swapping the order of the arguments (to match <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MvPolynomial.eval%E2%82%82Hom#doc\">docs#MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom</a>) result in a more natural definition?  If you flip the order, could the ideal be defined as the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=RingHom.ker#doc\">docs#RingHom.ker</a> of the hom?</li>\n</ul>",
